WEBVTT

00:01.640 --> 00:07.010
<i>The Imperial army, being harassed by
 the Federation's persistent attacks,</i>

00:07.010 --> 00:10.800
<i>recognized the right to self-rule
 by anti-government forces</i>

00:10.800 --> 00:13.280
<i>within occupied territories
 to stabilize the front.</i>

00:15.360 --> 00:17.560
A nice, warm coat.

00:17.930 --> 00:19.940
It's not your size! Give it to me!

00:19.940 --> 00:23.280
Calm down! There's enough for everybody!

00:20.710 --> 00:24.760
That's for tall people, not fat people!

00:25.480 --> 00:29.130
<i>It's hard to believe what we 
were going through last month.</i>

00:30.200 --> 00:34.530
<i>The Federation and Allied Kingdom 
expanded their cooperation,</i>

00:34.530 --> 00:37.210
<i>beginning a joint operation to the North.</i>

00:37.970 --> 00:42.000
Comrades, let us support our flank!

00:42.450 --> 00:44.570
In the name of international cooperation,

00:44.570 --> 00:48.450
how about a joint operation 
with the Allied Kingdom?

00:48.450 --> 00:53.610
Gentlemen, we will be launching 
a decoy operation to support allies.

00:54.120 --> 00:58.300
We will threaten the Imperial forces 
in the East by attacking their flank!

00:58.870 --> 01:03.570
<i>The Federation and Allied Kingdom 
strengthened their efforts</i>

01:03.570 --> 01:06.200
<i>to work with partisans in 
the former Entente Alliance.</i>

01:06.200 --> 01:10.410
<i>The Empire needed to respond fast,</i>

01:10.410 --> 01:12.990
<i>and sent the agile Salamander Combat Unit.</i>

01:18.030 --> 01:21.420
Damn it. Spring's a long way away.

01:22.450 --> 01:26.450
<i>We succeeded in driving 
the two enemies back.</i>

01:26.950 --> 01:29.520
<i>The Empire pulled back its reinforcements</i>

01:29.520 --> 01:32.340
<i>and decided to send them 
to the East once more.</i>

01:32.990 --> 01:36.300
<i>In the grand scheme of things, 
this was only a minor skirmish.</i>

01:37.020 --> 01:41.610
<i>But the Ildoa Kingdom was beginning 
to take action behind the scenes.</i>

03:12.960 --> 03:15.960
<b>Ildoa Kingdom Army Command</b>

03:14.700 --> 03:18.970
So the Empire was forced to 
send reinforcements to the North?

03:18.960 --> 03:23.970
<b>Ildoa Kingdom Mountain Unit
Colonel Igor Gassman</b>

03:18.970 --> 03:20.030
Correct.

03:20.030 --> 03:22.890
It seems that they're finding 
this rather costly.

03:22.890 --> 03:26.610
They're asking to pay for the high-octane 
fuel we're secretly providing them

03:23.970 --> 03:28.140
<b>Ildoa Kingdom Army Command
General Virginio Calandro</b>

03:26.610 --> 03:30.190
with things they've plundered 
during their operations.

03:30.190 --> 03:33.000
They're like a bunch of burglars.

03:30.230 --> 03:35.610
This story is a work of fiction. People, organizations, locations, laws, names, etc. have no relation to any real-life counterparts.

03:33.000 --> 03:35.610
Which means they're in dire straits.

03:35.980 --> 03:40.790
If we offer them help, 
we can put them in our debt.

03:40.790 --> 03:45.480
And if we can end this war, other 
countries will praise us endlessly.

03:46.140 --> 03:50.280
But will they listen to us?

03:50.280 --> 03:54.670
We simply have to leave them
no other choice.

03:54.670 --> 03:58.420
We must save our poor allies 
no matter what.

04:00.550 --> 04:04.550
<b>Episode Three:
Well-Intentioned Mediator</b>

04:04.550 --> 04:09.060
<b>Imperial Strategic HQ</b>

04:05.400 --> 04:09.060
Ildoa is doing a sudden 
mobilization exercise?

04:09.060 --> 04:11.770
We can assume the exercise is 
just what they said it would be,

04:11.770 --> 04:13.750
but we can't be too cautious.

04:13.750 --> 04:16.190
We might see another disaster 
like we saw with the Republic!

04:16.530 --> 04:19.510
Ildoa could be a threat,

04:19.510 --> 04:23.110
which means we need to drastically rethink
our strategy towards the Federation.

04:24.950 --> 04:29.770
I'd like to deliver those macaroni fuckers
straight into our enemy's hands.

04:30.080 --> 04:34.140
Agreed. But Ildoa is a valuable ally.

04:34.140 --> 04:36.510
It would be a poor idea 
to simply abandon them.

04:38.070 --> 04:42.620
If they are our allies, 
they'll allow us to send observers.

04:42.960 --> 04:45.830
I'll send Rerugen from our HQ.

04:45.830 --> 04:50.140
He'll see what there is 
to be seen, I'm sure.

04:57.980 --> 05:00.980
<b>Ildoa Guest Facility</b>

05:01.250 --> 05:03.610
I am General Virginio Calandro.

05:04.060 --> 05:09.400
Colonel Igor Gassman asked me 
to make sure you're settled.

05:10.000 --> 05:12.770
I'm honored, Colonel Calandro.

05:18.900 --> 05:22.810
<i>His hands are far too strong for him 
to be a mere political general.</i>

05:22.810 --> 05:25.260
<i>He's been on the battlefield 
many times, then.</i>

05:27.220 --> 05:32.060
I would love to be frank with 
you, since you're an ally.

05:32.060 --> 05:35.690
I'll skip the pleasantries.

05:36.230 --> 05:40.450
Ildoa is prepared to serve as 
a well-intentioned mediator

05:41.000 --> 05:44.150
and offer the gift of peace.

05:44.470 --> 05:46.150
Can you explain?

05:46.450 --> 05:50.170
Essentially, we wish to serve as 
mediators for peace negotiations.

05:51.430 --> 05:55.420
I'm sorry. Mediators for 
peace negotiations?

05:55.420 --> 05:56.840
Indeed.

05:56.840 --> 06:00.760
We're prepared to serve as 
a liaison between our friends.

06:00.760 --> 06:02.750
I may be overstepping myself here,

06:02.750 --> 06:05.770
but I believe you're looking 
for a way to end this war.

06:07.200 --> 06:11.360
Our leader back home would 
be the one to decide that.

06:13.050 --> 06:16.680
Of course, this is normally 
the job of a diplomat.

06:16.970 --> 06:20.980
But given the nature of our relationship,

06:20.980 --> 06:24.430
it seemed things would go smoother if 
we spoke to someone in the military.

06:25.190 --> 06:30.450
We've prepared to serve as a negotiator
between the empire and its foes.

06:30.920 --> 06:32.530
This is still internal,

06:32.530 --> 06:37.870
but we're also prepared to work with 
the States to jointly call for peace.

06:38.440 --> 06:42.860
I hope you'll understand 
what I mean when I say

06:42.860 --> 06:45.930
we speak from a position 
of considerable power.

06:46.500 --> 06:48.100
<i>I see...</i>

06:48.100 --> 06:52.420
<i>So that's the reason for this 
sudden mobilization exercise...</i>

06:53.730 --> 06:56.170
Those southern leeches!

06:56.170 --> 06:59.680
They're pretending to 
be neutral negotiators?

06:59.680 --> 07:03.440
If the conditions are right, 
it may be worth pursuing.

07:04.360 --> 07:10.450
And in the negotiations, we would 
want war reparations, I assume.

07:10.930 --> 07:15.910
We're preparing to accept 
Ildoan observers.

07:16.480 --> 07:21.010
And they'll use these to make 
decisions during the peace talks?

07:24.180 --> 07:27.490
<i>I want to find a way to 
bring this war to an end.</i>

07:27.960 --> 07:30.690
<i>No, I must find one.</i>

07:37.090 --> 07:38.880
Back to the east, huh?

07:38.880 --> 07:40.680
First snow, then mud.

07:40.680 --> 07:44.370
I keep washing my socks, 
and it doesn't help.

07:47.080 --> 07:49.810
We're stuck too far out in 
more places than I thought.

07:50.130 --> 07:52.700
Why don't they reorder the battle lines?

07:52.700 --> 07:55.440
They've made promises to 
the national councils.

07:55.820 --> 07:57.770
They can't retreat 
even if they want to.

08:01.020 --> 08:04.570
<i>I thought we were winning, 
and now we're back to losing.</i>

08:04.790 --> 08:09.090
<i>I guess I don't even have time to be 
thinking about saving my own ass.</i>

08:12.140 --> 08:18.160
<i>How do we find a way to end this war?</i>

08:21.090 --> 08:23.450
Lieutenant Colonel, a moment?

08:23.910 --> 08:26.030
What? What is it?

08:26.290 --> 08:28.910
Someone's here from Strategic HQ.

08:30.340 --> 08:33.320
It's been a long time, 
Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff.

08:33.320 --> 08:37.320
The coffee on the front lines has 
a whole different scent, you know.

08:37.320 --> 08:40.110
The Imperial stuff is 
just coffee-colored...

08:40.110 --> 08:44.070
Colonel Rerugen, what 
brings you here today?

08:45.610 --> 08:49.200
I was hoping to ask you 
to look after a guest.

08:49.610 --> 08:51.650
A colonel from Ildoa.

08:52.090 --> 08:54.410
A war observer?

08:54.410 --> 08:55.780
Indeed.

08:55.780 --> 09:00.090
Colonel, in our current state, 
we can't appropriately welcome him...

09:00.400 --> 09:01.720
I know, and I'm asking anyway.

09:03.830 --> 09:07.350
I see there must be 
something going on here.

09:08.770 --> 09:11.240
I'm sure you'll find out eventually.

09:11.240 --> 09:14.350
People's lips never stay 
sealed, after all.

09:16.260 --> 09:20.810
Today, I will become a mobile 
combat team commander,

09:20.810 --> 09:24.030
with the Salamander combat 
team serving under me.

09:24.880 --> 09:27.490
You'll be serving under me,

09:27.490 --> 09:31.970
but in fact, you will continue to 
serve as the actual commander.

09:31.970 --> 09:37.600
In other words, I am second in command 
of a non-existent Rerugen combat team,

09:37.600 --> 09:40.970
while commanding the actual 
Salamander combat team.

09:42.970 --> 09:44.640
Correct.

09:44.640 --> 09:47.720
But there is one thing I'm going 
to have to ask you to put up with.

09:48.480 --> 09:52.240
My name will be the one on 
the official combat reports.

09:52.910 --> 09:56.850
At least in the documentation, 
I will be stealing credit from you.

09:56.850 --> 10:00.570
Please... forgive me for this.

10:05.380 --> 10:08.340
<i>Someone takes over
 all responsibility on paper,</i>

10:08.340 --> 10:10.950
<i>and the guys in personnel owe me one?</i>

10:11.470 --> 10:13.970
<i>Hell yes.</i>

10:13.970 --> 10:15.540
<i>But still...</i>

10:17.220 --> 10:22.080
I am a soldier who has 
sworn to serve my country.

10:22.600 --> 10:26.440
I won't say I'm entirely 
on board with this...

10:26.440 --> 10:30.920
But I hope you can promise 
I'll be well taken-care of for this.

10:32.890 --> 10:34.690
I'm relieved.

10:34.690 --> 10:37.040
I was expecting you to shoot me.

10:38.660 --> 10:41.380
You're such a funny man.

10:45.780 --> 10:48.080
Hello, fräulein.

10:48.080 --> 10:51.330
I've been through it all, Colonel.

10:51.550 --> 10:54.430
My entire body has been 
covered with blood.

10:54.430 --> 10:58.420
Call me fräu, or Lieutenant Colonel, 
whatever you like.

11:00.630 --> 11:04.720
I am General Virginio Calandro.
 I've been sent here as an observer.

11:05.060 --> 11:07.690
Lieutenant Colonel Tanya von Degurechaff.

11:10.030 --> 11:13.550
I've heard you had 
the glorious Silver title,

11:13.550 --> 11:16.410
but I'm still surprised at 
your actual appearance.

11:16.410 --> 11:20.160
Less surface area means 
I'm harder to hit.

11:20.160 --> 11:22.400
Do watch out for stray bullets.

11:24.220 --> 11:25.800
I should, definitely.

11:25.800 --> 11:28.480
I'll crouch like this when 
I'm out on the battlefield.

11:29.800 --> 11:32.510
Welcome to the front lines.

11:33.310 --> 11:38.470
On behalf of your Imperial allies, 
I welcome you.

11:53.410 --> 11:55.410
You always get warm meals?

11:56.720 --> 11:59.520
Food affects morale.

11:59.520 --> 12:01.520
Eat while it's hot, Colonel.

12:05.470 --> 12:09.540
<i>Their forces are well-disciplined, 
even though we're on the front lines.</i>

12:10.760 --> 12:16.380
<i>I'm sure the Empire must be spending 
a fortune to maintain them.</i>

12:18.980 --> 12:20.800
What's the situation on our surroundings?

12:20.800 --> 12:25.350
Captain Ahrens just encountered 
an enemy tank group.

12:25.350 --> 12:26.430
I'm sorry,

12:27.070 --> 12:29.750
but may I be present for this discussion?

12:29.750 --> 12:31.680
Yes, of course.

12:31.980 --> 12:34.900
<i>Honestly, I'd prefer you 
fucked off, though.</i>

12:35.580 --> 12:38.330
You appear to be fighting 
in a residential area.

12:38.330 --> 12:40.370
How do you handle that?

12:40.370 --> 12:42.680
Artillery, I would say.

12:42.680 --> 12:45.890
Artillery? With no warning? 
Over a residential area?

12:45.890 --> 12:48.860
Yes. It should minimize casualties.

12:48.860 --> 12:53.540
Lieutenant Colonel, isn't that a 
violation of international wartime law?

12:53.800 --> 12:56.550
The convention you're referring 
to is reciprocal.

12:56.550 --> 13:01.180
It applies only when all parties 
to a war are signatories,

13:01.180 --> 13:04.050
and only to battles between said parties.

13:04.410 --> 13:09.140
As far as I'm aware, 
the Federation is not a signatory.

13:09.540 --> 13:11.950
Which makes it okay to burn a town?

13:12.400 --> 13:13.470
Yes.

13:13.470 --> 13:16.080
They've done the same to 
many Imperial cities.

13:16.080 --> 13:18.180
So the same fate awaits them.

13:18.580 --> 13:20.030
Wait!

13:20.030 --> 13:21.990
You're going to destroy a church?

13:21.990 --> 13:25.030
Attacks on religious personnel 
are a violation of wartime code!

13:25.420 --> 13:28.060
Hmm? I'm not sure I follow.

13:28.060 --> 13:30.990
Religious facilities and personnel 
are to be protected...

13:30.990 --> 13:32.910
We've confirmed the building lacks

13:32.910 --> 13:35.750
the markings required to designate 
it as a religious facility.

13:36.310 --> 13:37.550
What?

13:37.800 --> 13:42.090
We respect both military code 
and the laws of war.

13:42.090 --> 13:45.520
But the fact is, there's no mark there.

13:45.520 --> 13:48.050
But that's clearly...

13:50.180 --> 13:54.060
Do you see any kind of marking, Colonel?

13:56.970 --> 13:58.040
No.

14:18.740 --> 14:22.640
Thank you for your cooperation!

14:29.490 --> 14:32.310
You wanted to discuss something?

14:32.740 --> 14:35.810
I'll be quick. I want 
to ask you a question.

14:36.130 --> 14:39.070
I'll answer anything I can.

14:40.540 --> 14:44.830
I want to talk about how 
you see this war ending.

14:46.560 --> 14:48.520
That's why I'm here!

14:49.050 --> 14:52.680
<i>I see... so Ildoa is trying 
to serve as peace mediators?</i>

14:53.120 --> 14:56.780
<i>They'll give us the exit 
we've been looking for?</i>

14:57.230 --> 14:59.670
I'm sure it's hard to accept...

14:59.670 --> 15:01.920
But are you willing to make compromises?

15:02.240 --> 15:06.000
<i>Can I make compromises to 
get out of this mudhole?</i>

15:06.270 --> 15:08.170
<i>Hell yes, I can!</i>

15:08.170 --> 15:10.500
<i>Cut your losses! This is 
the time to cut your losses!</i>

15:10.500 --> 15:14.730
Would you tell us what the bare minimum 
conditions you'd be willing to accept are?

15:15.260 --> 15:17.840
Conditions? I don't have any.

15:17.840 --> 15:20.350
No conditions?

15:20.670 --> 15:23.080
I am a soldier.

15:23.080 --> 15:26.600
I swore a duty to obey any lawful order.

15:26.970 --> 15:30.610
If my leaders have decided 
on a way to end the war,

15:30.610 --> 15:34.120
I don't set conditions, I simply obey.

15:34.120 --> 15:39.490
My duty to obey lawful orders 
is my highest priority.

15:39.490 --> 15:42.350
That is what it means to be a soldier.

15:43.210 --> 15:44.830
I see.

15:44.830 --> 15:49.800
So the empire prioritizes the national 
interest, even on the front lines?

15:49.800 --> 15:51.080
Yes.

15:51.080 --> 15:54.790
Even the lowest commander 
at the front obeys!

15:54.790 --> 15:58.750
They are terrifyingly 
loyal to their orders!

15:59.170 --> 16:02.020
How can we persuade them...

16:02.020 --> 16:04.760
<i>Then they'll listen to us.</i>

16:05.140 --> 16:08.860
I see a way to make this mediation work.

16:08.860 --> 16:12.520
Now the war will end.

16:17.600 --> 16:22.950
<i>I got the war observer to understand that 
we Imperial soldiers are normal people.</i>

16:23.370 --> 16:27.460
<i>I'm sure the peace negotiations 
will go great.</i>

16:28.370 --> 16:30.670
<i>I did my work well.</i>

16:31.430 --> 16:34.790
<i>Now this war will end...</i>

16:39.470 --> 16:41.450
Lieutenant Colonel, may I have a moment?

16:41.450 --> 16:42.610
What?!

16:42.610 --> 16:43.470
What is it?

16:43.750 --> 16:46.340
A visitor from Strategic HQ...

16:46.780 --> 16:48.080
Again?!

16:49.390 --> 16:52.240
It's been a long time, 
Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff.

16:52.240 --> 16:56.230
It's been so long since 
I've had real coffee.

16:56.230 --> 16:59.370
The stuff back home looks 
like coffee, but...

16:59.370 --> 17:03.490
Lieutenant Colonel Ugar,
 what brings you here?

17:03.720 --> 17:06.630
We had some problems 
at a nearby railroad.

17:06.630 --> 17:09.470
While I was fixing them, 
I remembered my comrade

17:09.470 --> 17:11.630
from military school and 
decided to drop by.

17:12.370 --> 17:14.910
I see. I'm glad to hear that.

17:14.910 --> 17:16.550
This is my subordinate, Major Weiss.

17:16.550 --> 17:18.370
I thought he could join us.

17:19.280 --> 17:22.070
It's rare to see you with 
one of your subordinates.

17:22.450 --> 17:26.910
He's mostly here to keep 
listening ears away.

17:27.420 --> 17:28.720
What do you mean?

17:29.230 --> 17:34.080
I heard that Ildoa is 
working towards peace.

17:35.740 --> 17:38.240
You heard it too, then?

17:38.240 --> 17:44.130
They forced a war observer on me, 
and I was wondering why.

17:44.570 --> 17:47.140
The brass feels that we need

17:47.140 --> 17:50.740
to make some compromises to 
bring a swift end to the war?

17:51.050 --> 17:53.950
I hate it, but yes.

17:53.950 --> 17:57.000
We need to accept reality.

17:57.000 --> 18:01.520
I assume both sides will abandon 
demands for war reparations,

18:01.520 --> 18:03.210
abandon conquered territory,

18:03.210 --> 18:06.350
and restore borders to exactly what 
they were at the start of the war?

18:06.350 --> 18:10.330
They might even sign a treaty requiring 
all sides to shrink their armies.

18:10.330 --> 18:11.250
Lieutenant Colonel...

18:12.160 --> 18:14.600
That would not be peace with honor.

18:14.600 --> 18:16.310
It would be no different than surrender!

18:18.650 --> 18:23.490
Do you know how much money we've 
spent? How many lives we've lost?

18:23.490 --> 18:28.220
Doesn't that mean that the sooner 
we stop making sacrifices, the better?

18:28.220 --> 18:32.000
You would understand that 
better than anyone, I thought.

18:34.540 --> 18:37.520
What is your opinion, Major Weiss?

18:38.010 --> 18:40.830
I'd like to hear the thoughts 
of a frontline officer.

18:41.660 --> 18:44.250
M-May I speak?

18:44.250 --> 18:46.400
Go ahead. Speak.

18:48.230 --> 18:52.900
I would say that between
 a reward that justified the sacrifices,

18:52.900 --> 18:55.840
and a future where no more 
sacrifices needed to be made at all,

18:56.510 --> 18:58.210
I would choose the latter.

18:58.210 --> 18:58.990
Yes.

18:59.390 --> 19:00.470
But...

19:02.240 --> 19:03.650
I just can't accept it.

19:03.890 --> 19:05.040
What?

19:05.040 --> 19:09.130
To shed all this blood 
and end up with nothing at all...

19:09.130 --> 19:10.160
I just can't...

19:10.160 --> 19:11.990
Wait, wait, wait!

19:14.470 --> 19:18.210
I'm shocked... Even you feel that way?

19:18.720 --> 19:21.760
How can you accept it, Lieutenant Colonel?

19:21.760 --> 19:23.960
Because I have to!

19:23.960 --> 19:27.660
A frontline commander's job is knowing 
what to focus on and what to give up!

19:27.660 --> 19:29.890
If we have to cut our losses, 
then that's what we do.

19:30.600 --> 19:33.190
I'm sorry, ma'am, but that's just logic.

19:34.200 --> 19:36.410
It's... nothing but logic!

19:46.110 --> 19:47.690
<i>This is bad.</i>

19:47.690 --> 19:50.520
<i>Even my fellow soldiers and 
subordinates who I trust the most</i>

19:50.520 --> 19:53.090
<i>have fallen victim to 
the Concorde effect.</i>

19:54.230 --> 19:58.100
<i>From the look of things, 
Strategic HQ and the high leadership</i>

19:58.100 --> 20:01.180
<i>are going to have a hell of a time 
convincing the frontline soldiers.</i>

20:01.490 --> 20:04.430
<i>Will they have to crush them by force?</i>

20:04.430 --> 20:08.600
<i>Killing our own soldiers will look 
bad on my resume post-war...</i>

20:09.180 --> 20:11.180
<b>Imperial Strategic HQ</b>

20:11.170 --> 20:15.600
The Federation's demands have 
been relayed to us via Ildoa.

20:15.600 --> 20:18.070
They seek a ceasefire with no reparations,

20:18.070 --> 20:21.780
no territorial changes, 
and no additional conditions.

20:22.490 --> 20:24.290
Colonel Gassman,

20:24.690 --> 20:29.080
I have a message from command 
regarding the peace discussions.

20:29.080 --> 20:30.770
Let me hear it.

20:31.570 --> 20:36.370
They've rejected our demands, 
but negotiations are continuing.

20:36.370 --> 20:38.490
With enough time...

20:37.490 --> 20:39.440
You've gone soft.

20:39.440 --> 20:40.410
What?

20:41.200 --> 20:44.840
I said you've gone soft, Zettour.

20:45.610 --> 20:49.490
I've already talked to the high 
leadership regarding this.

20:50.000 --> 20:52.350
You can't have...

20:52.600 --> 20:56.350
I will share our nation's answer.

20:56.680 --> 20:57.830
Go on.

20:59.020 --> 21:00.400
"Eat shit."

21:00.770 --> 21:02.040
That is all.

21:03.840 --> 21:06.760
We will seize our destiny
 with our own fists.

21:06.760 --> 21:09.220
We will not put it
 in the hands of another.

21:09.880 --> 21:13.870
Our army's will is unyielding!

21:16.970 --> 21:19.780
We will begin Operation Iron Hammer!

22:50.260 --> 22:51.700
4th Company Commander!

22:51.700 --> 22:53.200
3rd Company Commander!

22:53.200 --> 22:54.390
2nd Company Commander!

22:54.390 --> 22:55.930
1st Company Commander!

22:58.020 --> 23:02.570
Wow, you people in the mage unit 
all got reassigned, huh?

23:02.570 --> 23:05.480
Huh? Then Major Weiss is...

23:05.480 --> 23:08.860
Replacing Lieutenant Colonel Degurechaff,
 since she now runs the combat team.

23:09.390 --> 23:12.060
He's in charge of all the mages.

23:12.060 --> 23:15.030
That's amazing! Congratulations!

23:14.450 --> 23:15.570
Shut up!

23:19.330 --> 23:21.280
Wh-Why?

23:21.280 --> 23:25.440
Actually, losing the position of company 
commander means less bonus pay...

23:25.440 --> 23:28.590
And he has to pay out of pocket for 
stuff to keep the unit running.

23:28.590 --> 23:30.970
His take-home pay has 
actually gone down.

23:31.480 --> 23:34.250
Promotions are scary...

23:35.970 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time
Operation Iron Hammer</b>
